---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"{short_help}\\n--- LONG ---\\n{long_help}\\n--- TOOL ---\\n{tool_help}\")"
---
Search indexed items and check service health

Usage: my-tools [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  search-items  Searches indexed items
  http-server   Checks service health

Options:
      --output <MODE>       Selects artifacts, structured, raw, or binary output [default: artifacts] [possible values: artifacts, structured, raw, binary]
      --images <MODE>       Controls Kitty image display in artifact output [default: auto] [possible values: auto, kitty, off]
      --artifact-dir <DIR>  Parent directory for artifact output
      --input-json <TOOL>   Reads the selected tool's JSON object from stdin [possible values: search-items, http-server]
  -h, --help                Print help (see more with '--help')
  -V, --version             Print version

Use --help for the full reference.

--- LONG ---
Search indexed items and check service health

Search by query and refine results with filters.

Use fast mode for interactive searches.

Usage: my-tools [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  search-items  Searches indexed items
  http-server   Checks service health

Options:
      --output <MODE>
          Selects output: artifacts renders text and saves binary blocks; structured writes structuredContent JSON; raw writes the complete MCP result as JSON; binary writes exactly one decoded binary block. Output options must precede the command.
          
          [default: artifacts]
          [possible values: artifacts, structured, raw, binary]

      --images <MODE>
          Controls Kitty image display in artifact output
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, kitty, off]

      --artifact-dir <DIR>
          Parent directory for artifact output. A private unique invocation directory is created beneath it.

      --input-json <TOOL>
          Selects a command and reads exactly one complete JSON object from standard input through EOF. Cannot be combined with a command subcommand.
          
          [possible values: search-items, http-server]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

--- TOOL ---
Searches indexed items

Usage: search-items [OPTIONS] --mode <STRING> --query <STRING>

Options:
      --mode <STRING>
          Search strategy.
          
          [possible values: fast, thorough]

      --query <STRING>
          Search expression.

      --environment <JSON>
          Process environment. Value is strict JSON (object); JSON strings require quotes.

      --filter-range-min <INTEGER>
          Smallest accepted value. Required when `filter` is activated. Format: int64.

      --filter-range-max <INTEGER>
          Largest accepted value. Format: int64.

      --filter-tags <STRING>
          Labels to include. Repeat this option once per array item; order is preserved.

      --input-json <STRING>
          A property sharing the root adapter option's spelling.

      --limit <INTEGER>
          Optional result limit. Format: uint64. Minimum: 0.

      --recursive [<BOOL>]
          Whether to recurse. Accepts --option, --option=true, or --option=false forms.
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --rules <JSON>
          Ordered matching rules. Value is strict JSON (array); JSON strings require quotes.

      --threshold <NUMBER>
          Optional score threshold. Format: double.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
